ard write selects the link (`copyOrSelect.ts`, shared with `ServerMenu`). Keys in every box field go through `rangeKeys.ts` `boxKeydown`: `Mod-Enter` submits and `Escape` cancels (built with `keys.ts` `keyList`, matched by `pressesKey`; only the composing check is its own) (a draft is dropped, a reply cleared), both `preventDefault` and `stopPropagation`; every other key stays the field's. `RangeApp` calls `fileListKey(event, navigator.platform)` as the other roots do; the reply's Comment keeps focus in the reply field (`@mousedown.prevent`). `RangeSendButton.vue` sits left of the gear in each `RangeView` header; `RangeApp` shows the last send's result (`sendNoticeRow`) as a closable `NoticeBar` row and passes each file's thread count to `RangeFileRow` (a muted speech bubble, none at 0).
 
 Edit and Delete (plan §2 #123): `rangeNoteChange.ts` holds both rules — `isChangeable` (a note not pending) decides whether `RangeMessage.vue` shows them, and `noteChangeBlock(sending, aiTurn)` (a send running first, then the thread's AI turn) turns them and Save off, with `noteChangeTitle`'s hover text. Edit writes an `edit` draft (`rangeDrafts.ts` `editDraft`/`writeEdit`/`dropEdit`), shown in the message's place by `RangeMessageEditor.vue` (`box="edit"`, label "Comment text", Save; its `offTitle` is the block's title); writing an `edit` draft drops the message's `post` draft and the reverse, so the two boxes are never open at once. `editNote` sends only a non-blank text and drops the draft when stored; focus returns to Edit after Save or Cancel. Delete goes through `rangeStore`'s `deleteNote`, which asks `{ kind: "deleteNote" }` first. Every list a reply brings (`setList`) drops the open state and the reply, Post and Edit drafts of threads and messages it no longer holds, and the Edit draft of a note no longer changeable (a Send that made it pending closes its box), so a thread removed with its last note leaves nothing behind.
